<%# How much of it there is, in the bar on the way to Settings. Server-rendered so the line
    is right before any JavaScript runs and right on a post nobody types into; the bar
    controller rewrites the spans as the body grows. The unit word rides as data because it
    is the one that changes with the number, and the copy stays Ruby's on both passes.
    A canvas with nothing in it says "0 words" and nothing about minutes: the one-minute
    floor is a promise made to a reader, not a counter for the writer. %>
<% words = word_count(post) %>
<p class="editor-bar__count" data-bar-target="count" data-word-one="word" data-word-many="words">
  <span data-bar-target="words"><%= number_with_delimiter(words) %></span>
  <span data-bar-target="wordUnit"><%= "word".pluralize(words) %></span><span
    data-bar-target="pace"<%= " hidden" if words.zero? %>> · <span data-bar-target="minutes"><%= reading_time(post) %></span> min</span>
</p>
